A||||4||Gold-86SE||Is that SMOKE I see? Yep, it is!!||||1||
Z||000000||Gold-86SE||09-14-2000||11:39 PM||||<BR>Sorry for the length, but I wanted to share my story from Thursday.<P>So I start my 84 this morning, getting ready to head off to work.  It starts and then quits.  Ummm? That's not normal it must be an omen.  Well forget it, I'll take the 86 Fiero and worry about it later.<P>So I get home in the evening and about 7pm head up town to buy subway (descent eats btw) and as I am heading up a hill, I feel the 84 jerk and bump.  Now, that's way not normal.  So I pull it out of 4th and let it coast in neutral for a several feet, trying to get a feel for what is going on.  Everything feels okay, so I put in back in gear and continue on up the road until I am stopped by a red light.<P>At the light, I make a strong effort to examine the engine area for any signs of malcontent - none found, the light turns green so I proceed forth.  I am crossing the bridge coming to the next intersection, scanning to my right for other cars that might want to join my lane of traffic after their yeild sign, and what do I see in the corner of my right eye?  Blue smoke, thick blue smoke.  AAAAHHHHHHHHHH!!!!!! I'm on fire.<P>The first thing that went through my head was I just read on the forum where one guy has a fire extinguisher in all his Fieros, here I am on fire and without one - it's a gonner for sure.  So I pull into the parking lot, stop the car, open the rear deck expecting billowing clouds of smoke and... nothing.  I mean absolutely nothing.<P>Okay, I saw the smoke, what's wrong here.  I look over the engine looking for signs of problems and what do I find?  A twisted belt.<P>So I see this guy at the gas station, who is filling up his Ford F250 dually, figuring to myself, this guy has to have a few tools. I speak with him and he has what I need and I head back to my Fiero while he heads inside to pay for his fuel.<P>So I loosen the alternator and find that the belts was thrown, and man was it mangled.  Burned down to the belts in some places and totally bent in others. It's a wonder it did not come of the engine.<P>I returned the tools to this gentleman, ask him for a ride, he gives me a lift to my house.  I pick up my tools, an extra belt, drive back to the dead 84, fix it and drive home.  Then I ask my Pontiac loving neighbor to give me a lift back to my newly repaired 84 and I drive it home.  Man, what an evening.  Sure am glad I did not take it to work that morning.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||09-15-2000||12:12 AM||||PHEWWW!!! Man I thought I was gonna hear yet ANOTHER "Fiero on fire" story! Glad to hear it was only the belt!<BR>BTW, I was the one who stated that I keep an extinquisher in all of my Fieros...I did it originally as a joke, due to all the Fiero-ignorant people who say "dont those things catch on fire"..after I give them the standard "small percent of 84s/ 4 cylinders only" speech, I then show them the extinquisher in the car and grin.<BR>But I am glad I have them in my cars!||||reg||1
Z||000002||HugGRRRFiero||09-15-2000||08:28 AM||||I keep a fire extinguisher in my 84, mainly for grins, but hey, you never know when you might have to use it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>This spring I had an alternator belt literally explode on me, shredded but the belt stayed on.  It made one heck of an aweful noise slinging around back there.  I used a spare the previous owner left in the trunk area, bad choice, it was old and the next day stretched turning my car again into a battery powered air-cooled engine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||7
Z||000003||DJRice||09-15-2000||10:11 AM||||Back when I first returned my 84SE to road worthy condition I was driving it to work one day and missed a shift or something.  Well, I ended up twisting a belt all up too but for a few short moments I thought I killed the car.  I got the smoke and some wierd noises, but it turns out that the AC belt got all twisted up and then broke.  Luckily, it didnt take the other belt with it and I was able to go on to work without the benefit of A/C.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierospeeder||09-15-2000||10:37 AM||||I had an oil leak and it got on my 84 fiero's belt.  I was driving one day and noticed my engine temp rising very quickly.  <P>I pulled over, pop the front hood, and see coolant gooing all over.  Looked at the engine, and found that i had no belt.  I had a cop sort of harass me because i wasn't suppose to park there, and i asked him if he wanted me to move.  He said no its fine.<P>I was about 3 miles away from home, and i saw a rag in my trunk and teared it up.  I tied it in a circle and used it over the waterpump and pulley.  It got me about three blocks until the rag would come off.  Eventually i got to trak auto.  Went home, got my tools and put in a new belt.||||reg||1
